        h2 Release Notes

        p
          | Stay up to date with the latest firmware updates, software improvements, and new features for all Baldrick products.

        .callout.info
          span.ic
            svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
              circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"
              path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"
          div
            span.lbl Update notification
            p.bd Your board should alert you when a new update is available. Not all updates are available for all boards.

        h3#release-history Releases

        .rn-entry#v3-8-4
          .rn-entry-head
            h4 3.8.4
            span.rn-badge Latest release

          h5.rn-label What's new
          ul.mb-8
            li Support for 5 channel pixels
            li Reduced crashiness, generally (specifically in CunningFX)
            li Fix busk mode on FPP proxy
            li Some people had some very specific issues in the firmware that would only affect them.. we've fixed them.

        .rn-entry#v3-8-3
          .rn-entry-head
            h4 3.8.3

          h5.rn-label What's new
          ul.mb-8
            li We did a bunch of fixes to crashes we detected

        .rn-entry#v3-8-2
          .rn-entry-head
            h4 3.8.2

          h5.rn-label What's new
          ul.mb-8
            li Busk Board now works on Chrome
            li Busk Board now allows you to set multiple actions to a button press
            li Improved Signals WiFi
            li Multiple crash fixes
            li Add 802.11r support (helps when moving the board between mesh APs)
            li Improved efficiency of WiFi memory usage

        .rn-entry#v3-8-1
          .rn-entry-head
            h4 3.8.1

          h5.rn-label What's new
          ul.mb-8
            li Actions can now be triggered on Signals visitor numbers
            li Multiple Actions can now be triggered at the same time
            li Busk Board button now added to Desktop
            li The interface should load properly on Mac now...
            li Dom left some code in for localStorage... bad Dom

        .rn-entry#v3-8-0
          .rn-entry-head
            h4 3.8

          h5.rn-label What's new
          ul.mb-8
            li ArtNet fixes, especially around ArtSync (most people won't care)
            li Fixed CunningFX start via the Turnip Network, can you believe someone actually wanted to us a feature we made!
            li PURDY Logo in the header
            li Added Vendor Class Identifier (VCI) to DHCP requests (even more people won't care)
            li Added Busk Board to mobile / tablet view.

        .rn-entry#v3-7-1
          .rn-entry-head
            h4 3.7.1

          h5.rn-label What's new
          ul.mb-8
            li Fixed issue with Signals that caused problems with data logging and downloads.
            li You can now set custom lock-out times for input buttons.
            li You can now set input buttons to remain locked out until explicitly unlocked with an HTTP call
            li You can now lock out all input buttons on a board when one is pressed.
            li Fixed issue with Signals that caused problems with data logging and downloads.
            li When activating a relay from a button, you can now set a custom activation time.
            li Fixed JS loading issues on FPP Proxy
            li Added debug download link

        .rn-entry#v3-7-0
          .rn-entry-head
            h4 3.7 - Don't go chasing Protocols

          h5.rn-label What's new
          ul.mb-8
            li • Added support for UCS1903, SM16703P & UCS2904 pixel types.
            li • Added Static IP Mode to all boards
            li • Added Network reset mode to all non pixel boards.
            li • LLDP support - No one will care, but we now have LLDP support

          h5.rn-label Special modes
          p Each board now has three special modes that you can activate with button presses:

          .rn-grid.rn-grid--3
            .rn-subcard
              h6 Reset to factory settings
              p Resets the board to factory settings, because sometimes you break it so much, the only way to make progress is to begin again.
            .rn-subcard
              h6 Reset network settings
              p Sometimes you only break it MOSTLY and doing this will reset JUST the network settings.
            .rn-subcard
              h6 Set static IP
              p
                | Sometimes you don't have a DHCP server and you need the damn board to appear on the network (and we don't want to deal with 169. addresses). This sets the IP address to
                strong  192.168.68.68
                | .

          h5.rn-label How to activate
          .rn-stack
            .rn-subcard
              h6 Baldrick8 & Baldrick17
              p
                | Press and hold a certain button and power cycle the board. Hold
                strong  B1
                |  for about 10 seconds to reset network settings,
                strong  B2
                |  to set a static IP address, and
                strong  B3
                |  for a reset to factory settings.
            .rn-subcard
              h6 All other boards
              p
                | Press and hold the 'oh no' button and power cycle for about 10 seconds to reset to factory settings. Press 'oh no'
                strong  3 times in 3 seconds
                |  to reset network settings, or
                strong  5 times in 3 seconds
                |  to set the static IP address.

          .rn-subcard
            h5.rn-label Frequently asked (ish) questions
            .rn-stack
              div
                p
                  strong Why can't I set the static IP address it resets to?
                p HOW… A COMBINATION OF DOTS AND DASHES ON THE OH NO BUTTON.. GET A GRIP SAMANTHA, WHY CAN'T YOU JUST BE HAPPY THAT WE CREATED A FEATURE YOU WANTED, WHY IS IT NEVER GOOD ENOUGH?? WHY??..
              div
                p
                  strong Why 192.168.68.68?
                p Three reasons: 1) it works better on Dom's local network, 2) ending in 168.68.68 is easy to remember, 3) he couldn't get an IP that worked with 8008135.
        .rn-entry#v3-6-0
            h4 3.6 - Signalling the start of Christmas
            ul
              li This update will only affect the BaldrickSignals, if you don't have one, you don't need to update (but updating won't break anything)
              li The BaldrickSignals is now using the same firmware branch as it's brothers and sisters! 
              li We've added the modifiers in to allow you to account for visitors without mobile phones and those devices that are always in your vicinity .
              li The graph library has changed and theres now a download data button to get the data in CSV, JSON or XML format. 
              li 
                b As the title suggests we will soon be implementing our seasonal freeze period, where only URGENT fixes are released via the main channel but we've got one more update first.
        .rn-entry#v3-5-4
          h4 3.5.4 - Test Mode Stability 
          ul
            li If you enabled test mode and refreshed and refreshed and refreshed and refreshed and refreshed and refreshed and refreshed and refreshed and refreshed and refreshed and refreshed and refreshed the page it would cause a bit of an issue with the board, I don't know why someone would want to do this but they did, reported the issue and we've fixed it the best we can.
            li I'm going to have to add please don't use the web interface like ticketmaster on Taylor Swift ticket release day to the docs aren't I?    
        .rn-entry#v3-5-3-0
          h4 3.5.3.0 - Internal 
          ul
            li  This release is for our internal monitoring system for board testing, normally we can hide these changes within other updates but some of the things we are testing require us to do a production release.
            li This is not a required update, don't rush out to do it, it will change NOTHING for you.
        .rn-entry#v3-5-3
          h4 3.5.3 - Testing My Patience 
          ul
            li  More Universal Addressing modifications (This time with Artnet)
            li  Our new build system was not including the JS files, this was an issue for anyone wanting to use the boards web UI. 
            li  Test mode will now default to 50 pixels per port if there are no models and all configured models if not.
            li  We've moved the pixel amount box to the top because people kept missing it.
        .rn-entry#v3-5-2
          h4 3.5.2 - Internal
          ul
            li  This release is for an internal system fix and was not available for public download.            
        .rn-entry#v3-5-1
          h4 3.5.1
          ul
            li  RGBW uploads from xLights should now be in the correct order, the reason this took so long for us to fix is that nobody has bought Dom any RGBW pixels.
            li  ⁠CunningFX will now switch betwen effects rather than just toggling.
            li  ⁠More Absolute Universe addressing changes, we still aren't fully announcing this feature yet as it needs some changes but it's been requested and people are using it.
            li  ⁠DHCP will no longer report BALDRICKBOARD as the hostname everytime.
            li  ⁠Allow people to update when on FPP Proxy 

        .rn-entry#v3-5-0
          h4 3.5.0 - Ghost of Pixels Past
          ul
            li Turns out when people opt into the beta release, it really didn't want you to opt out, you now can.
            li The BaldrickDMX board had an issue with test mode, Dom used this as an excuse to buy a new smoke machine to test it and now it's fixed.
            li Input1 can finally control CunningFX on other boards, please stop messaging me now. 
            li Michael Floyd reported an issue with the B17 and large config files with lots of models, that is now fixed after our initial suggestion of buying more boards to have one port per port was ignored
            li Unlike previous updates, we will actually let people on the Baldrick8 update to this one! (someone forgot to tick a checkbox last time)

        .rn-entry#v3-5
          h4 3.5 - Quality of afterlife improvements.. 
          ul
            li Pressing and holding B1 for 5 seconds on boot will now reset network settings on both the B17 and B8. 
            li The updates we made to the Input8 last time for multiple FPP instances are now available for all boards. 
            li Some people using annoying pixel colour orders were complaining that they were not working, so we did an intense overview of the firmware and realised someone got the GBR mixed up with BGR but it's all sorted now.
            li We've added some performance improvements to the B17, I know this sounds like a generic app update description but there are so many little tweaks that Pete listed to me, I'll admit I switched off and started scrolling TikTok. 
            li Test mode now defaults to the first 50 pixels rather than all configured pixels, this should reduce my support tickets by about 30%.
            li We now stop you adding hostnames with spaces in them, because it tends to break things. 
            li In the VERY VERY slight chance that your board crashes, it sends a small crash report to us with what happened. 
            li Sometimes the B17 would say that a system update was available, but it wasn't. We've taken the board to one side and told it that it needs to sort itself out.
            
        .rn-entry#v3-4-0
          h4 3.4.0 - Augustly Delivered
          ul
            li Pixel Extrodinare August Thede reported a bug with the input8 board and multiple FPP instances and we were SHOCKED, SHOCKED I TELL YOU!.. Once we'd recovered from the horror that our board had a software issue, we realised that it was a simple fix and we've released it to you all.
            li You may be wondering why the jump from 3.1.0 to 3.4.0 and we were wondering why you were wondering, if we had a good answer for this we'd have obviously told you.
